    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "B*Ai $ / JAPAN AIR LINES.\nSAFETY INSTRUCTIONS\n76701\nEMI TAKE-OFF AND LANDING\nBAGGAGE\nPlace baggage in the overhead bins or under a seat.\nPlease stow baggage securely.\n83 2\nFASTEN SEATBELT TIGHT AND LOW Keep seat belt fastened whenever seated.\n*Li* To fasten\nTo tighten\nTo unfasten\nSEAT POSITION\nSet seat back\nand table in\nupright position.\nNO SMOKING\nRefrain from\nsmoking in\nrestrooms or\naisles.\nTEA BRACE POSITIONS",
      "EMERGENCY EXITS\nB\nDIDA\nFERO EXIT\n00000000000000000000000 00\n#E*D EXIT\n#*#*0É FOR EVACUATION\nDo not carry any baggage.\nRemove highheeled shoes.\nPut out cigarettes before evacuating.\n-0-0-0-0-0-0-0\nME 1J DO NOT REMOVE FROM AIRCRAFT",
      "B*Ai $ / JAPAN AIR LINES\n167N0\nSAFETY INSTRUCTIONS\nФорАБИ LIFE VEST\nInflate when instructed by a crew member.\n2\n3\n4\nLife vest under seat.\n5\n6\n8\nFor extra inflation blow into\nTo Inflate.\npieces.\n57*0580Xİ TO FIT THE LIFE VEST TO A CHILD\n2\n3\nmouth\nPull string to light emergency bea-\ncon.\nPass the straps between\nthe legs and secure\nin front.\n•*******Infant life vests provided by crew members.\n*7ZD OXYGEN MASK\nOxygen mask will appear automatically when needed.\nPut out your cigarette immediately. PULL\nAdults accompanied by small childlen should secure thier own mask first."
    ],
